# text = She had no permanent consciousness of other fetters , or of more spiritual restraints , having always disliked whatever was presented to her under the name of religion , in the same way that some people dislike arithmetic and accounts : it had raised no other emotion in her , no alarm , no longing ; so that the question whether she believed it had not occurred to her any more than it had occurred to her to inquire into the conditions of colonial property and banking , on which , as she had had many opportunities of knowing , the family fortune was dependent .
