# text = Rex would have seemed a vision of his father's youth , if it had been possible to imagine Mr . Gascoigne without distinct plans and without command , smitten with a heart sorrow , and having no more notion of concealment than a sick animal ; and Anna was a tiny copy of Rex , with hair drawn back and knotted , her face following his in its changes of expression , as if they had one soul between them Rex began , and Mr . Gascoigne nodded Mr . Gascoigne nodded more slowly , the perpendicular line on his brow deepened , and Anna's trembling increased Rex thought the vagueness of the phrase prudential ; " the colonies " necessarily embracing more advantages , and being less capable of being rebutted on a single ground than any particular settlement said Anna , not bearing to be left out from the proposal even temporarily Anna had risen from her seat , and used the feminine argument of going closer to her papa as she spoke .
