# text = There was a considerable pause before Grandcourt said , looking toward her Gwendolen did not turn her eyes on him ; it seemed to her a long while that she was first blushing , and then turning pale , but to Grandcourt's rate of judgment she answered soon enough , with the lightest flute-tone and a careless movement of the head She checked her horse as she spoke , and turned in her saddle , looking toward the advancing carriage .
