# text = Diplow lay in another county , and was a comparatively landless place which had come into the family from a rich lawyer on the female side who wore the perruque of the restoration ; whereas the Mallingers had the grant of Monk's Topping under Henry the Eighth , and ages before had held the neighboring lands of King's Topping , tracing indeed their origin to a certain Hugues le Malingre , who came in with the Conqueror -- and also apparently with a sickly complexion which had been happily corrected in his descendants .
