# text = Deronda's thinking went on in rapid images of what might be : he saw himself guided by some official scout into a dingy street ; he entered through a dim doorway , and saw a hawk-eyed woman , rough-headed , and unwashed , cheapening a hungry girl's last bit of finery ; or in some quarter only the more hideous for being smarter , he found himself under the breath of a young Jew talkative and familiar , willing to show his acquaintance with gentlemen's tastes , and not fastidious in any transactions with which they would favor him -- and so on through the brief chapter of his experience in this kind .
