# text = After that they joined the girls in the other room , where Mirah was seated placidly , while the others were telling her what they knew about Mr . Deronda -- his goodness to Hans , and all the virtues that Hans had reported of him said Mab said Mirah , smiling at Mab , and appealing to the graver Amy said Amy said Mirah , with her usual quietness said Amy , rather suspicious of this sentiment , and on the watch for Jewish peculiarities which had not appeared said Kate When he entered , Mirah rose with the same look of grateful reverence that she had lifted to him the evening before : impossible to see a creature freer at once from embarrassment and boldness .
