# text = Her mother thought Gwendolen would have been rather angry if that thought had been uttered ; perhaps all the more because through the last twenty hours , with a brief interruption of sleep , she had been so occupied with perpetually alternating images and arguments for and against the possibility of her marrying Grandcourt , that the conclusion which she had determined on beforehand ceased to have any hold on her consciousness : the alternate dip of counterbalancing thoughts begotten of counterbalancing desires had brought her into a state in which no conclusion could look fixed to her .
