# text = Formerly when he had asked Lydia to put them into his keeping again , simply on the ground that they would be safer and ought to be deposited at the bank , she had quietly but absolutely refused , declaring that they were quite safe ; and at last had said At that time Grandcourt had no motive which urged him to persist , and he had this grace in him , that the disposition to exercise power either by cowing or disappointing others or exciting in them a rage which they dared not express -- a disposition which was active in him as other propensities became languid -- had always been in abeyance before Lydia .
