# text = The most powerful movement of feeling with a liturgy is the prayer which seeks for nothing special , but is a yearning to escape from the limitations of our own weakness and an invocation of all Good to enter and abide with us ; or else a self-oblivious lifting up of Gladness , a _Gloria in excelsis_ that such Good exists ; both the yearning and the exaltation gathering their utmost force from the sense of communion in a form which has expressed them both , for long generations of struggling fellow-men .
