# text = Deronda began by looking at her , but felt himself presently covering his eyes with his hand , wanting to seclude the melody in darkness ; then he refrained from what might seem oddity , and was ready to meet the look of mute appeal which she turned toward him at the end he said , gratefully she said , with a smile of delight said Deronda Mirah smiled with a touch of merriment he had not seen in her before here she turned so as to take all three of her companions in one glance said Deronda , smiling She went on willingly , singing with ready memory various things by Gordigiani and Schubert ; then , when she had left the piano , Mab said , entreatingly said Mirah said Deronda said Mrs .
