# text = Meyrick said Deronda said Mirah Deronda shook his head Mirah crossed her little feet and hands in her easiest attitude , and then lifted up her head at an angle which seemed to be directed to some invisible face bent over her , while she sang a little hymn of quaint melancholy intervals , with syllables that really seemed childish lisping to her audience ; the voice in which she gave it forth had gathered even a sweeter , more cooing tenderness than was heard in her other songs said Mirah , when she had repeated the hymn several times said Deronda said Mrs .
