# text = A man in threadbare clothing , whose age was difficult to guess -- from the dead yellowish flatness of the flesh , something like an old ivory carving -- was seated on a stool against some bookshelves that projected beyond the short counter , doing nothing more remarkable than reading yesterday's _Times_ ; but when he let the paper rest on his lap and looked at the incoming customer , the thought glanced through Deronda that precisely such a physiognomy as that might possibly have been seen in a prophet of the Exile , or in some New Hebrew poet of the mediaeval time .
