# text = Here Sir Hugo and Grandcourt turned round and paused said Gwendolen said Sir Hugo , glancing at Deronda said Gwendolen , bending her head and smiling said Sir Hugo , looking at the husband said Grandcourt , without change of countenance All this seemed to Sir Hugo a natural playfulness between such a husband and wife ; but Deronda wondered at the misleading alternations in Gwendolen's manner , which at one moment seemed to excite sympathy by childlike indiscretion , at another to repel it by proud concealment .
