# text = Hans , too , was silent for a minute , took up his palette and began touching the picture on his easel he said at last said Deronda , more coldly than was usual with him said Hans , decisively Hans , still with pencil and palette in hand , had moved to Deronda's side while he said this , but he added hastily , as if conscious of a mistake said Deronda said Hans , his face creasing drolly said Deronda said Hans Here Hans pretended to speak with a gasping sense of sublimity , and drew back his head with a frown , as if looking for a like impression on Deronda said Deronda , after a moment's contemplation Neither of them had yet mentioned Mirah said Hans , putting touches to his picture said Deronda , not knowing exactly how to express his discontent Here Hans went a little way off and looked at the effect of his touches said Deronda , feeling more indignation than he would have been able to justify said Deronda , chiefly in order to hinder himself from saying something else said Hans After Deronda had been turning over the drawings a minute or two , he said said Deronda , holding up a drawing said Deronda , holding up a sketch of the Trasteverina said Hans , looking at it rather contemptuously Deronda was silent while he closed the folio , leaving the Trasteverina outside .
