# text = When the wherry was approaching Blackfriars Bridge , where Deronda meant to land , it was half-past four , and the gray day was dying gloriously , its western clouds all broken into narrowing purple strata before a wide - spreading saffron clearness , which in the sky had a monumental calm , but on the river , with its changing objects , was reflected as a luminous movement , the alternate flash of ripples or currents , the sudden glow of the brown sail , the passage of laden barges from blackness into color , making an active response to that brooding glory .
