# text = He had sunk into momentary darkness said Deronda , in a clear deep voice which was itself a cordial , apart from the words of sympathy said Mordecai , quickly , looking up again with the flash of recovered memory and confidence Mordecai had taken a step nearer as he spoke , and now laid his hand on Deronda's arm with a tight grasp ; his face little more than a foot off had something like a pale flame in it -- an intensity of reliance that acted as a peremptory claim , while he went on Deronda had become as pallid as Mordecai .
