# text = Before him stood , as a living , suffering reality , what hitherto he had only seen as an effort of imagination , which , in its comparative faintness , yet carried a suspicion , of being exaggerated : a man steeped in poverty and obscurity , weakened by disease , consciously within the shadow of advancing death , but living an intense life in an invisible past and future , careless of his personal lot , except for its possible making some obstruction to a conceived good which he would never share except as a brief inward vision -- a day afar off , whose sun would never warm him , but into which he threw his soul's desire , with a passion often wanting to the personal motives of healthy youth .
# sent_id = 4079
