# text = Gwendolen had not caught sight of Deronda in her passage , and while she was seated acquitting herself in chat with Sir Hugo , she glanced round her with careful ease , bowing a recognition here and there , and fearful lest an anxious-looking exploration in search of Deronda might be observed by her husband , and afterward rebuked as something But all traveling , even that of a slow gradual glance round a room , brings a liability to undesired encounters , and amongst the eyes that met Gwendolen's , forcing her into a slight bow , were those of the Mr . Lush , whom Sir Hugo continued to find useful as a half-caste among gentlemen .
