# text = Gwendolen's inclination lingered over the project of the singing lessons as a sort of obedience to Deronda's advice , but day followed day with that want of perceived leisure which belongs to lives where there is no work to mark off intervals ; and the continual liability to Grandcourt's presence and surveillance seemed to flatten every effort to the level of the boredom which his manner expressed ; his negative mind was as diffusive as fog , clinging to all objects , and spoiling all contact .
