# text = We know little about the grounds of mutual discontent between the Siennese couple , but we may infer with some confidence that the husband had never been a very delightful companion , and that on the flats of the Maremma his disagreeable manners had a background which threw them out remarkably ; whence in his desire to punish his wife to the unmost , the nature of things was so far against him that in relieving himself of her he could not avoid making the relief mutual .
