# text = But in no concealment had she now any confidence : her vision of what she had to dread took more decidedly than ever the form of some fiercely impulsive deed , committed as in a dream that she would instantaneously wake from to find the effects real though the images had been false : to find death under her hands , but instead of darkness , daylight ; instead of satisfied hatred , the dismay of guilt ; instead of freedom , the palsy of a new terror -- a white dead face from which she was forever trying to flee and forever held back .
