# text = Inarticulate prayers , no more definite than a cry , often swept out from her into the vast silence , unbroken except by her husband's breathing or the plash of the wave or the creaking of the masts ; but if ever she thought of definite help , it took the form of Deronda's presence and words , of the sympathy he might have for her , of the direction he might give her .
