# text = Deronda did not formally say But simply , instead of packing and ringing for his bill , he sat doing nothing at all , while his mind went to the synagogue and saw faces there probably little different from those of his grandfather's time , and heard the Spanish-Hebrew liturgy which had lasted through the seasons of wandering generations like a plant with wandering seed , that gives the far-off lands a kinship to the exile's home -- while , also , his mind went toward Gwendolen , with anxious remembrance of what had been , and with a half-admitted impression that it would be hardness in him willingly to go away at once without making some effort , in spite of Grandcourt's probable dislike , to manifest the continuance of his sympathy with her since their abrupt parting .
