# text = We should be churlish creatures if we could have no joy in our fellow-mortals' joy , unless it were in agreement with our theory of righteous distribution and our highest ideal of human good : what sour corners our mouths would get -- our eyes , what frozen glances ! and all the while our own possessions and desires would not exactly adjust themselves to our ideal .
