# text = Even a man who has practised himself in love-making till his own glibness has rendered him sceptical , may at last be overtaken by the lover's awe -- may tremble , stammer , and show other signs of recovered sensibility no more in the range of his acquired talents than pins and needles after numbness : how much more may that energetic timidity possess a man whose inward history has cherished his susceptibilities instead of dulling them , and has kept all the language of passion fresh and rooted as the lovely leafage about the hill-side spring !
