# text = It seemed to him really the more graceful course for a widow to recover her spirits on finding that her husband had not dealt as handsomely by her as he might have done ; it was the testator's fault if he compromised all her grief at his departure by giving a testamentary reason for it , so that she might be supposed to look sad , not because he had left her , but because he had left her poor .
