# text = There was a dreamy , sunny stillness over the hedgeless fields stretching to the boundary of poplars ; and to Gwendolen the talk within the carriage seemed only to make the dreamland larger with an indistinct region of coal-pits , and a purgatorial Gadsmere which she would never visit ; till at her mother's words , this mingled , dozing view seemed to dissolve and give way to a more wakeful vision of Offendene and Pennicote under their cooler lights .
