# text = The familiar objects around him , from Lady Mallinger's gently smiling portrait to the also human and urbane faces of the lions on the pilasters of the chimney - piece , seemed almost to belong to a previous state of existence which he was revisiting in memory only , not in reality ; so deep and transforming had been the impressions he had lately experienced , so new were the conditions under which he found himself in the house he had been accustomed to think of as a home -- standing with his hat in his hand awaiting the entrance of a young creature whose life had also been undergoing a transformation -- a tragic transformation toward a wavering result , in which he felt with apprehensiveness that his own action was still bound up .
